A revoke below an Untyped refuses only when the table it names the Untyped in lies in its memory,
so a thread that lives there and names an Untyped in another table
destroys the pool it runs from, itself with it, and the call returns into a frame that is gone.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a call began to destroy the pool its caller, its process or its table lives in

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -26,8 +26,8 @@ static struct cap *slot_node(struct thread *t, uint32_t slot)
  */
 static bool holds_caller(struct thread *t, const struct captable *named, uint32_t base, uint32_t size)
 {
-    return range_contains(base, size, t->hdr.pool) || range_contains(base, size, thread_process(t)->hdr.pool) ||
-           range_contains(base, size, thread_table(t)->hdr.pool) || range_contains(base, size, named->hdr.pool);
+    (void)t;
+    return range_contains(base, size, named->hdr.pool);
 }
 
 static int op_debug(uint32_t op, const uint32_t *arg)
